  explanation: "Variation across Australia: ~0\u20132\u00b0E in WA to ~12\u201313\u00b0E in eastern states. A cross-country flight must use the applicable variation for each segment. Using eastern variation for a western leg (or vice versa) introduces systematic heading errors. Chart isogonals show the variation for any location.",
